The bundled Rover Base template (templates/rover-base/main.tex.njk) is
adapted from Rover resume templates by subidit:
https://github.com/subidit/rover-resume
Original template: templates/base rover/base-rover.tex
Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
modified: converted to Vita's template contract, parameterized layout and
replaced sample content with resume data; removed pdfTeX-only primitives.
The adapted template retains the CC BY 4.0 licence.

Additional bundled Rover adaptations (each main.tex.njk and template.yaml):
- rover-star: templates/star rover/star-rover.tex
- rover-fancy: templates/fancy rover/fancy-rover.tex
- rover-milky: templates/milky rover/milky-rover.tex
- rover-office: templates/office rover/office-rover.tex (sample photo removed)
- rover-obsolete: templates/obsolete rover/obsolete-rover.tex and preamble.tex
  (preamble inlined)
- rover-academic: templates/academic rover/acad-few.tex and acad-many.tex
  (one academic design; publications come from resume sections, not BibTeX)
- rover-week-monday, rover-week-tuesday, rover-week-wednesday,
  rover-week-thursday, rover-week-sunday: corresponding day .tex files in
  templates/week rover/. All five supplied day designs are retained; the
  upstream checkout has no Friday or Saturday file.

These templates are by subidit, from https://github.com/subidit/rover-resume,
licensed under CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ .
Modifications: Vita contract placeholders, parameterized layout, safe empty
optional fields, explicit list indentation, microtype, no paragraph indent,
XeTeX-compatible primitives, dynamic footer names, and publication data in
place of bibliography files. Week Tuesday uses a safe red heading instead
of the original fixed-three-token splitter for arbitrary section titles.
The adaptations retain CC BY 4.0. Their preview.png files show the fictional
Vita developer fixture rendered using the adapted templates.
